WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.790
Mr. Penguin's Dilemma!

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.050
Hello!

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:43.910
What's wrong?

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.000
It's a battlefield.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.530
Battlefield?

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.390
A-Anyway, do you guys 
want to order something?

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.350
You need to choose!

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:04.940
Choose!

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.270
Y-You're right...

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.960
All right, who wants the cake set?

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:17.070
We're not talking about the menu!

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.700
We're saying that you need 
to choose one of us!

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.200
One of us!

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.400
They've got him cornered.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.660
Indeed.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.620
Yeah, what a haul!

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.050
I can't eat any more!

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.060
I think his soul has 
wandered off somewhere.

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:50.260
It must be hard for him.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.230
Each of them have their own unique features.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:58.510
You can tell the 
Penkos apart, Mr. Llama?

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.690
You mean you can't?

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.280
What's different about them?

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.700
Look.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.330
The slim one is Miss Penko.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:11.470
The one with a unusually shaped 
beak is Miss Penmi.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.530
Miss Penna is slightly boyish.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.720
Miss Penka is slightly coquettish.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.280
Miss Penno is a Japanese beauty.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.930
The sexiest is Miss Pennuelle,

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.410
and Miss Penjolina is the 
easiest to differentiate.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.690
Her beak is plump.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.570
They all look exactly the same to me.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.140
That's hard to believe.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.540
I thought those ribbons were

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.700
supposed to help with 
telling them apart.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.290
It appears that they're trading 
them every now and then.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.110
Oh, here it comes.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.080
Hey, are you listening?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.830
Are you listening?

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.590
Y-Yes...

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:01.080
You're able to 
tell us apart now, right?

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.130
O-Of course!

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:09.030
I see. In that case, who am I?

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:10.980
Huh?

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:12.860
What about me?

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:13.920
And me?

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.940
And me?

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:16.840
And me?

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:17.720
And me?

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:18.900
And me?

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.860
U-Um...

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:28.280
If you make a mistake, 
you'll be sorry.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:34.160
I wonder if we should 
be leaving them alone.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:34.750
Huh?

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.160
I hear that female emperor penguins

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:42.020
brutally fight over male 
emperor penguins.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.100
A fight would not be good.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.520
Miss Sasako, please give 
this memo to Mr. Penguin.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.320
Huh?

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.380
Now say which one I am.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:58.180
U-Um...

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:02.410
Pardon the interruption, 
but are you ready to order?

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:03.990
Oh, we're sorry.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.910
I wonder what I should get?

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.730
I want to get a parfait.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.920
Here, Mr. Penguin.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:11.870
What?

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:21.800
Penko 
Penmi 
Penka 
Penno 
Penna 
Penjolina 
Pennuelle

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:21.800
Red 
Blue 
White 
Yellow 
Purple 
Green 
Pink

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.820
Thank you for your order.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:25.920
It will be out shortly.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:26.760
Okay.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:29.880
Good luck.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:30.640
Thanks!

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:36.230
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.190
Now say which one I am.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.520
You're...

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.550
Miss Penko, aren't you?!

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.110
Huh?

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.570
Yes, I am.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.950
And you're Miss Penmi!

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:52.530
Huh?

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.950
Yes, I am!

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:57.960
You're Miss Penno!

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.920
I am.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.920
You're Miss Penna!

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:03.510
Yes.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.920
And you're Miss Penka!

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:07.440
Yes!

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:10.260
And you're Miss Pennuelle!

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:12.810
What?

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.510
Oh, my mistake.

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:17.090
Um...

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:19.430
Huh? Miss Pennuelle is...

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:22.840
Red is Miss Penko, 
white is Miss Penka.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:25.700
Miss Penmi is blue...

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.280
Huh?

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:45.520
Let's try this one more time...

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.190
Looks like the plan failed.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:55.140
In the end they did a shuffle.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.180
There's nothing more that can be done.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.180
This is too troublesome.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.630
They should just go out 
with you, Mr. Llama.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:04.320
Quiet. Mr. Penguin 
is making his move.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.610
What's in a name?

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.570
What?!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.470
I didn't fall in love with your names!

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:25.360
I love you all for who you are, 
just the way you are!

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:32.140
He's cornered, so he's
 going with a power move.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:34.640
Hopefully he'll be able to escape.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.680
That's right!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.110
What point is there in me saying

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:39.580
who is who right now?

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:42.060
There's none. 
There's no point at all!

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:46.020
Your feathers are not beautiful 
because of your name!

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:49.960
Existence itself is what is beautiful!

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:52.490
Yes, just like all of you.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:56.010
Oh... Oh my.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:01.680
So please, don't concern yourself 
with such trivial matters.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.020
Just feel the love!

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.020
<i>Did it work?</i>

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.010
All right.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.840
Huh? Really?

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.720
So, who will it be?

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.810
Oh. That's right.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.650
You're absolutely right.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:28.850
It was no use.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.110
That would have been too easy.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.990
If things continue like this...

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.910
Ow, ow, ow, Pe-Penm—

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.930
Ow, Penk— Ow, Pennu—

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:47.880
Like Shura

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:49.990
Things will end like that.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.860
Please stop with the 
weird exaggerations.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.280
All right, Miss Sasako. 
Please go stop them.

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:56.010
Huh?

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:02.600
I'm scared...

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.530
You go, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:06.770
According to my grandma's will,

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:10.320
I can't come out from behind 
the counter right now.

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:12.770
That's a terrible lie.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:14.200
How about you go, Mr. Llama?

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.130
Panda's already over there.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.280
What?

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.240
Excuse me, could I have a moment?

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:22.780
What?!

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:29.880
P-Panda, you don't need 
to be here! Go away!

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.170
What do you like about Mr. Penguin?

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:33.690
Huh?

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:38.070
I still don't know what's 
so good about Mr. Penguin,

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.640
so I'm really interested.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:44.100
Well, he took me to a 
fun amusement park.

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:51.220
This is so exciting, 
isn't it, Mr. Penguin?!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:56.500
Huh?

00:09:56.500 --> 00:10:00.580
Let's see... 
Well, he took me to karaoke.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:04.880
I'm on fire with songs from the 90's!

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.510
It ain't gonna stop!

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:08.920
Ain't no one gonna stop me!

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.840
All right, here we go. 
The Avex 90's songs...

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.000
Huh?

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.420
Well, you know.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.800
He took me out to a wonderful dinner.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.520
One more bottle!

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.610
Let's get another bottle over here!

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:32.650
Huh?

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.610
Other than that...

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:40.040
It'll be hard to meet 
with you separately...

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:43.040
So from now on, let's all meet 
together. All together!

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:43.780
Okay?

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:48.730
Huh? Why do I like him?

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:50.830
No kidding.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.790
The more I think about it, 
why do we even like him?

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:58.220
Th-That's because there was 
something good about me, right?

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:05.140
Y-Yes?

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:07.520
Goodbye.

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:11.100
What?!

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:14.610
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.750
We should probably let him be.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:26.780
Yeah.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:29.960
Hey.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:34.540
Is there not a single 
good thing about me?

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.420
Oh, you were worried about that?

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:42.070
I think not having any is what's
 good about you, Mr. Penguin.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:44.410
There has to be at least one.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.390
No, there have to be lots!

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.390
Now, now.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.490
At least your dilemma is over with.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:51.850
Cheers!

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.490
Thanks for all your hard work.

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:55.360
Hey, wait a minute!

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.740
All right. Let's toss 
Mr. Penguin up in the air.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.110
Ready and...

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:00.160
There has to be something—

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:04.050
Heave ho, heave ho.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:02.140
Don't change the subject.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.010
Too high!

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:09.910
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:08.560
Idol: Yama Arashi!

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:14.380
Apparently Yama Arashi is 
really hot right now.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:16.080
What the hell is that?

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:18.700
It's a popular idol group.

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:23.410
It's a group of five porcupines and 
they're super popular with girls.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:27.100
My mom is hooked on them, too.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:35.170
I wonder when she was cursed 
into liking porcupines.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:38.250
I think she just genuinely likes them.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:42.490
Panda

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.490
I'm home.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.450
Man, I'm tired.

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:49.310
You just got home. What's the matter?

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:53.120
Let me laze around for
 the little time I have off.

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:56.390
You only work twice a week.

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:59.290
You have more days off 
than days you work.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:02.820
Pandas are allowed to laze around.

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.620
You're in the way of my cleaning.

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.300
And you should be cleaning your room.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:10.670
Well if I clean it, 
you'll have less to do,

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:13.400
so I'll leave it for you.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:20.240
Don't suck me up!

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:27.350
I wonder if he's so lazy 
because I spoiled him.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.990
Maybe I should kick him 
out of the house once.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:34.530
Go live on your own.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.150
What?!

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:40.920
But knowing him...

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.840
Please give me bamboo. 
It will make me happy.

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:44.840
Even as a stray panda, 
he'd laze around.

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:54.850
Completely different from the sharp 
members of Yama Arashi.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.800
Oh, hello, Ms. King Penguin.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.660
It's finally tomorrow!

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:07.700
It is!

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:11.240
The Yama Arashi concert!

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:15.910
I heard that the Capybara Kids are going
 to be the backup dancers this time!

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.320
Capybara? I haven't heard of them.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:21.250
They're absolutely lovely 
and refreshing.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:24.490
All right. I'll look them up.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.350
Well then, I'll meet you 
at the station tomorrow.

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.340
See you.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:32.720
capybara

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:32.720
Let's see...

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:34.500
I wonder if this is it.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:41.150
This is... a capybara?

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.110
Look how long his upper lip is.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:46.070
Not to mention he's buck-toothed 
and not very cute.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:50.340
Something so short and 
stout can become an idol?

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:54.390
Then my son could have 
become an idol, too!

00:14:56.570 --> 00:14:58.060
And then he could have been

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:01.000
a backup dancer for 
Yama Arashi by now...

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.500
One, two, three...

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:06.140
And he would know the members...

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.390
Hello, I'm Panda's mother.

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:09.230
Oh, hello.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:14.430
My chance to get close 
to Yama Arashi...

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:18.800
I {/i1}was{/i0} wrong in how I raised him!

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.440
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:24.360
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:27.820
Panda

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:27.820
I'm going now.

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:31.740
Oh, by the way, 
I'll be home late tonight.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:36.240
I made some bamboo shoot stew for dinner,

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.110
so just warm it in the microwave.

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:39.410
Okay.

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:40.790
Where are you going?

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:45.040
To the Yama Arashi concert!

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:47.710
Oh, that's right.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:50.220
Looking for Animal Talent!!

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:50.220
You too can be a future idol!
Short-term courses available!!

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:50.220
Musician Course
Talent Course
Acting Course
Seiyuu Course

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:49.780
Here.

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:51.850
Talent?

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:53.430
What's this?

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:58.130
I don't think it's too late 
for you to become an idol.

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:02.210
But I'm already an idol at the zoo.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.690
But all you do is laze around.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:09.360
Idols have to be able 
to dance and sing!

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:13.160
But me lazing around is 
what everyone likes.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:19.110
Sorry to keep you waiting, 
Ms. King Penguin.

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.820
Oh, Panda Mama!

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:25.120
Don't you look lovely!

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:27.000
Can you tell?

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:30.570
I made sure my brushing 
was thorough today.

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:32.430
Me, too!

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:35.250
I was so excited last night 
that I couldn't sleep!

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:38.010
I know! Me, too!

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:46.250
It's so crowded.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.900
All of these people are 
headed to the Dome.

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:57.480
Look at all these people!

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.500
Let's go buy merchandise first!

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:00.160
Let's!

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:05.050
Wow, so much event-only merchandise!

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:08.710
A poster and tour book is a must.

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.460
Not to mention a fan 
and a pen light...

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:16.390
T-Shirt

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:15.730
Oh, but I want a clear 
file folder and T-shirt, too.

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:20.500
Oh, whatever! I'm going to buy it all!

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:21.750
I'll have the lot!

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:24.280
Oh, throw a bag in, too!

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.460
I can't believe I spent so much...

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:32.320
It's for a good cause! 
It had to be done.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.610
You're right. This is a must 
if you're a true fan.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:37.130
Oh, Panda Mama.

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:40.670
You originally couldn't even tell 
the difference between

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.950
Canadian Porcupine and Crested Porcupine.

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:44.630
I know!

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:49.880
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:51.640
Wow!

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.660
I'm amazed at how huge the Dome 
is each time I come here.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:05.710
I better eat now, while 
I have the chance.

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:10.110
I'm going to get 
ready to cheer.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:15.260
The pen light on this 
tour is delightful.

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:18.920
You can even change how it lights up.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.630
Oh, really?

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:25.250
You can set it to flash to go 
along with the up-tempo songs,

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:29.920
and then set it to wave 
for the slow ballads.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.210
You're right!

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:41.050
Arashi! Arashi!

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.350
Everyone's getting excited!

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:47.080
All the girls are so excited!

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:50.670
We may not have the 
energy of these girls,

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:52.790
but let's do our best 
to cheer them on, too!

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:53.650
Yes!

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:13.020
Yama Arashi!

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:24.810
Oh, aren't they...

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.820
The Capybara Kids.

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:28.270
They're cuter than I thought they'd be.

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:32.810
<i>Are you ready?</i>

00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:36.530
<i>We're going to take you</i>

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:40.550
<i>To the night-time savanna</i>

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:45.070
P-Panda Mama! Here comes their solos!

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:46.950
<i>We are nocturnal, tonight!</i>

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:50.540
<i>Were you surprised?</i>

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:53.850
Canada!

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:54.440
<i>The spikes on our backs</i>

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.960
<i>Aren't just for show</i>

00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:00.410
Crested!

00:19:57.640 --> 00:20:01.110
<i>We're going to stir up a storm</i>

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:01.950
<i>Yama</i>

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:05.320
<i>A-ra-shi</i>

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:05.320
A-ra-shi!

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:11.430
<i>Even though we're small</i>

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:14.060
<i>We're unstoppable!</i>

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:14.060
Unstoppable!

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:17.170
<i>Drum with our feet</i>

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:20.100
<i>Hit with our spines</i>

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:22.340
Oh, my gosh! Crested totally 
looked right at me!

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:26.240
<i>Even lions will run away</i>

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:25.510
He totally looked at me, too!

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:29.970
<i>That's right, we are</i>

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:32.870
<i>Yama A-ra-shi</i>

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:32.870
A-ra-shi!

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.240
Everyone's pen lights look so pretty.

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:41.180
This sense of togetherness 
is so amazing.

00:21:10.340 --> 00:21:13.130
Everyone, thanks for coming today!

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:15.290
We'll see each other again soon!

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:17.850
Of course!

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:20.680
We'll come again!

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:24.720
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:24.720
End of line

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:24.720
Enlarged Image

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:30.370
They were all so cool.

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:32.780
I've become an even bigger fan!

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:34.310
You get to forget about

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:36.890
house work and kids just for a moment.

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:38.110
I know.

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:43.960
<i>Thank you for making me feel 
young again, Yama Arashi.</i>

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:59.810
My mom went to a concert yesterday.

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:01.040
The Yama Arashi concert?

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.240
Yup.

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:05.630
How about we start an idol group, too?

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:06.840
Don't think that's possible.

00:22:07.450 --> 00:22:09.720
You can be our manager, Miss Sasako.

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:18.440
Thank you, everyone!

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:23.440
Why's the manager outshining 
everyone else?

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:58.040
Building

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:25.600
Next Time

00:23:58.470 --> 00:23:59.910
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:00.960
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:03.380
How long do you want to be 
unemployed, Mr. Penguin?

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:05.590
I don't think I want to be 
unemployed in general.

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:07.570
You're so strange, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:07.570 --> 00:24:09.410
I think you're the one that's strange.

00:24:09.410 --> 00:24:11.740
Then what do you want 
to be? A stink bug?

00:24:11.740 --> 00:24:13.300
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:14.550
Let's continue a little longer.

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:15.850
Please, end it.

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:17.710
Next week's Polar Bear's Café

00:24:17.710 --> 00:24:19.390
will be something presented somewhere.

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:21.410
That's entirely too vague.

00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:22.450
Enjoy!

00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:24.510
The Café Garden
Sales Penguin's Sales
